{"id":"u-8c8281a7-272e-429e-a8c0-e9ef58f8f809","src":"community","title":"WAVEFORGE: 12-Week Strength Cycle","author":"Sara M.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/HHZJAt-untitled-program","desc":"The program combines structured barbell strength work with progressive weighted pull-ups, optional conditioning and rotating accessories to build strength, athleticism and long-term progression without unnecessary volume.\n\nWeekly Structure\n\nDay 1 — Main Strength Day\nThe first primary strength session of the week, focused on Back Squat, Bench Press and Weighted Pull-Ups, followed by a rotating accessory or superset.\n\nDay 2 — Optional Strength + Conditioning\nA complementary session built around Overhead Press and Power Clean. This day is intentionally optional and can be skipped when recovery, time or conditioning demands require it. A short WOD can be added after the strength work when appropriate.\n\nDay 3 — Main Strength Day\nThe second primary strength session, focused on Front Squat and Deadlift, followed by a rotating accessory or superset.\n\nDay 1 and Day 3 are the foundation of the program. Day 2 is flexible and should complement—not interfere with—the main strength sessions.\n\nOther Training Days\n\nOn the remaining days, the program can be complemented with:\n\n* One conditioning/circuit day\n* One mobility + bodyweight/pull-up skills day\n* Core: twice per week, preferably after training sessions\n\nThe goal is to create a flexible weekly structure where strength remains the priority while conditioning, running, mobility and bodyweight skills can be integrated around it.\n\nProgramming Philosophy\n\nThe program uses wave-based periodization rather than repeating the same intensity week after week.\n\nEach wave gradually moves from higher-volume work toward heavier, lower-rep strength work, followed by a deload before beginning the next wave at a higher level.","level":["Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Strength","Athletics","Muscle"],"equipment":["